WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.550
With the return of Deadpool's Wade Wilson
comes a whole new set of faces that will join

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:09.080
the hero in his fight against evil in Deadpool
2 and a new standout has taken the Internet

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:09.740
by storm.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.160
Meet Peter, played by Rob Delaney.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.300
On the surface, Peter is your average middleaged
dude.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.560
But it seems that what he lacks in super powers,
he makes up for with enthusiasm.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.460
Rob Delaney may be a new face in the comic
book movies, but this isn't his first rodeo.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:28.680
Let's take a closer look at why Peter from
Deadpool 2 looks so darn familiar.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:29.900
"You're in."

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.980
Funniest Person on Twitter

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.780
Back before Twitter expanded its character
limit from 140 to 280, Delaney regularly used

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:44.460
the social media platform to workshop material,
bringing witty quips and humorous observations

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.860
to the Internet before it was the fashionable
thing to do.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.180
In 2012, Delaney became the first person to
be named "The Funniest Person on Twitter"

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.980
at Comedy Central's Comedy Awards.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.660
Delaney explained his social media success
to Mashable, saying,

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.720
"Don't work too hard on a tweet.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.549
[...] When you see people trying to, for example,
synthesize two current news stories into one

00:01:04.549 --> 00:01:08.929
'clever' tweet, it can get pretty clunky and
their labor is obvious, rendering their tweet

00:01:08.929 --> 00:01:09.429
unfunny."

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.540
Published author

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:16.500
In 2013, Delaney released a memoir titled,
Rob Delaney: Mother.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:17.240
Wife.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:17.860
Sister.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:18.420
Human.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:19.100
Warrior.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:19.880
Falcon.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:20.500
Yardstick.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.180
Turban.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:21.820
Cabbage.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.760
While the book featured its fair share of
dad humor and fart jokes, Delaney also used

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.620
the medium to explore his very real struggles
with depression and alcohol addiction.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.550
A decade before he honed his craft online,
he was regularly bombing on stage, and he

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.380
made a habit of getting blackoutdrunk.

00:01:37.789 --> 00:01:42.160
With his book, Delaney returns to the rock
bottom moments that helped shape the man he's

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:42.660
become.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:44.440
Delaney told The L.A. Times,

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:48.799
"[It] was a memoir that paid no attention
to chronology and was just about memories

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.300
that surfaced in my own, sort of, psyche.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:54.840
Because I figured those would be the ones
that would be most interesting to people."

00:01:55.149 --> 00:01:58.620
"Yeah, I drove into a building in LA, uhhuh.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.800
And broke both my arms and was in jail, in
a wheelchair."

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:03.420
Standup

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:09.560
According to an interview with Good Men Project,
Delaney's life changed in 2009 after he was

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.480
arrested for driving under the influence.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:16.620
He got sober, and about a year later, he began
seriously pursuing standup comedy.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.640
The comedian explained,

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.280
"Honesty is the main ingredient.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:24.280
I mean, you must be funny, but certainly the
funniest stuff will always be the most honest.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.280
No secret there."

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:30.780
Delaney has since played shows all over the
country, and eventually landed his own 2013

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:33.400
comedy special Rob Delaney: Live at the Bowery
Ballroom.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:38.760
"Now, if you see someone with a neck tattoo,
you know that they got it at their local muffin

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:39.260
shop.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.520
They got like a frappuccino neck tattoo special."

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:44.320
TV roles

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:49.280
Over the years, Delaney has continued racking
up credits both behind and in front of the

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:49.780
camera.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:54.519
For a short time, he had a project in the
works at Comedy Central called "At Rob Delaney,"

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.640
which unfortunately never saw the light of
day.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:01.180
As he continued flexing his comedic muscles,
Delaney found himself graduating from the

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:06.340
confines of the Internet and eventually landing
in the posh arena of primetime network television,

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.160
appearing in shows like Cougar Town and Burning
Love.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:14.050
The funnyman also appeared in multiple sketches
on Comedy Central's Key &amp; Peele, with his

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:16.940
standout performance being the Campaign Advisor
character.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:19.140
Catastrophe

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.140
In 2014, Delaney relocated his family to the
UK.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.280
"I love it, I love living there, and their
teeth are… a mess."

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:32.010
According to the Los Angeles Times, just one
year after settling into his new home, the

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:37.430
hit series Catastrophe premiered on Britain's
Channel 4 and, soon after, Amazon Prime's

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:38.160
streaming platform.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:43.859
The Emmynominated, BAFTAwinning series is
cocreated and cowritten by Delaney and Sharon

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:44.360
Horgan.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.180
"Thank you Sharon Horgan for teaching me how
to write comedy.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:52.700
I could do standup, I could tell a joke but
not make a show, thank you!"

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:57.019
Not only did the series disrupt the romcom
formula with a pleasant amount of vulgarity

00:03:57.019 --> 00:04:01.620
throughout the realistic subject matter came
at audiences with a brutal sense of honesty

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.480
seldom seen on the small screen.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:08.660
Variety reported back in 2016 that the streaming
service renewed Catastrophe through its fourth

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:09.160
season.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.100
UK star

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.440
One of the perks of being the Funniest Person
on Twitter is the global audience that the

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.440
platform provides.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:20.380
Once Delaney relocated to Britain, his star
only continued to rise.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:25.280
In between his time as a fulltime comedian,
TV star, and writer, Delaney has made a habit

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:29.690
of appearing on a handful of British panel
shows, a popular type of game show that throws

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:30.620
celebrities into the mix.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:35.911
Throughout his experience doing standup comedy
and pontificating on pop culture online, Delaney

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.140
has proven himself to be a worthy competitor.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:39.620
Thanks for watching!

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.480
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.750
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

